From 4b0c754fdd45093d01a297314a164d58099016cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:58:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add social links and owner info note to the place detail page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Renders Telegram / TikTok / Instagram links and a free-text info block
(opening hours, days off, announcements) on places-detail, with a
community submission path behind admin moderation.

- Social row: one tile per platform in three states — connected (opens
  the profile, with a pencil for suggesting a correction), empty (opens
  the submit sheet), and awaiting review.
- Info note: rendered with textContent and white-space: pre-line, so a
  stored note keeps its line breaks without any markup being built from
  user input.
- One bottom sheet serves all four fields, following the prayer settings
  sheet idiom: scrim, grab handle, drag-to-dismiss, Escape, backdrop tap
  and Telegram BackButton.
- Submissions POST to /api/place/<id>/submit with the signed initData in
  X-Init-Data. A submitted value is never rendered as live: on success
  the field flips to "waiting for review" and a toast confirms it.
- Server rejection codes map to localised copy, so users see their own
  language rather than the API's English.

Also applies the page's existing data-i18n attributes, which were
declared but never processed — the loading, error and retry strings were
stuck in Uzbek in every language.

51 new i18n keys across uz/ru/en; every server error code has a message.
No changes to css/style.css.
